      {
        "review_id": 464295225,
        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r464295225-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "Great learning experience but...",
        "text": "It was one of a good visit here. We were approached at the gate by a guide named Richard. I must tell you how awesome he was. He spoke very good English very clearly and of course his history knowledge is really great. Learned a lot from him. We were worried how much would the guide cost at the end of our tour as he seemed very professional. But he only charged NPR1000 each and it was pretty worth it. But be a little careful while taking photos with the Sadhus. They ripped us off NPR1500 just for few photos. I'd rather pay that to the guide! My husband gave NPR500 and they said more so I took NPR1000 when one asked for another 500. He then said he had change. When I handed the money over he said that's it. But well, its a once in a lifetime experience and I guess as tourists, sometimes we dont have much options in a foreign land not knowing if we had rejected, what would happen. But overall, was good to learn. Beware of the dust and smoke from cremation thou.",
